To build on Mac OS X
1) Install dependencies listed in 'dependencies.txt'
2) mkdir build
   cd build
   qmake ..
   make
3) make install     # Install resources into .app bundle

*Should* be cross platform, but different build rules must be written for the
different platforms.

For older versions of QT, I had to use custom build specs so that c++11 features
were brought in:
   qmake -spec ../build_specs/macx-g++47 -o Makefile ../CSGFEM.pro
   make

   Or, for clang:
   qmake -spec /opt/local/share/qt4/mkspecs/unsupported/macx-clang ../CSGFEM.pro

================================================================================
Results File Format (Binary)
All integers are 64-bit, all floating point numbers are doubles
================================================================================
RESULT_2D    (magic ASCII number)
Result Name  (null-terminated string)
Gridcell_overlaps.size()
Gridcell_overlaps (sequence of doubles)
Model Name     (null-terminated string)
Model:
    BBox: vector, vector
    null-terminated json string
Settings Name  (null-terminated string)
Settings       (null-terminated string)
NumElements NumNodes NumBoundary    (not strictly needed because we have
                                     cell overlaps, but simplifies parsing)
NumFields (NF)
NF { Field Type (NODE_SCALAR, NODE_VECTOR, ELEM_SCALAR, ELEM_VECTOR)
*  {    FieldData

================================================================================
Running on the HPC cluster.
================================================================================
There are some oddities with the modules on the HPC cluster, but the following
seems to work:
Include in .bash_profile:
    module load eigen/3.0.5
    module load suitesparse/intel/3.6.1
    module load gcc/4.7.3 
    module load intel/11.1.046 
    export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$LD_LIBRARY_PATH:$HOME/usr/lib
$ make -f MakefileBowery
